# The test-health runs that run nowhere else while ADR 0135 keeps GitHub
# Actions to the Release suite (TESTING.md, After merge): `just test-health`
# (ci/test-health/scheduled.sh) on `main`'s head, in the backstop's gate
# worktree, whose lock keeps them apart from the backstop and from each
# other. They go into the gate host's crontab (`crontab -e`), with
# GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT set to the main checkout. Times are UTC, after the
# backstop's 03:37 start, which #2094 adds as ci/gate-backstop.crontab; a run that finds the
# worktree busy or the disk short lists itself as skipped in
# ~/test-health/results.txt and fails. Each starts `origin/main`'s script, not
# the checkout's, which nothing fast-forwards; the script then runs the scripts
# of the commit it tests. The post-merge run has no line here: each `just
# merge` gate starts it as it ends (ci/merge-pr.sh, #2619).
GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT=/Users/jb/Dev/goodfetch
# ADR 0072's mutation testing, advisory: the Rust `main` changed in the last
# 24 hours, daily, within 150 minutes.
47 6 * * * bash -lc 'cd "$GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT" && git fetch --quiet origin && script=$(git show origin/main:ci/test-health/scheduled.sh) && nice -n 10 bash -c "$script" scheduled mutants origin/main'
# The constrained test-health run (ADR 0064): the Pre-merge suite on half the
# CPU and memory, a fresh order seed, weekly on Sundays, within 120 minutes.
17 9 * * 0 bash -lc 'cd "$GOODFETCH_CHECKOUT" && git fetch --quiet origin && script=$(git show origin/main:ci/test-health/scheduled.sh) && nice -n 10 bash -c "$script" scheduled constrained origin/main'
